      "Server Authority: Server is authoritative for movement, collision, interactions, inventory, guard states, puzzle logic, and transitions.",
      "One Carried Item: A player may carry at most one item. Pickup, drop, and handoff operations are atomic server-side transactions.",
      "Safe Disconnect Drop: Items held by a disconnecting player return to the nearest valid grounded platform directly below them; items are never destroyed or duplicated.",
      "Room Persistence: Visited room states (opened boxes, moved panels, deployed ropes, cut hatches) persist throughout the campaign session.",
      "Guaranteed Critical Items: Mandatory progression items (Room 9 cutting tool, keys) have fixed, non-randomized locations.",
      "No Irreversible Softlocks: Every puzzle has an anti-softlock recovery route. No puzzle requires permanent capture, impossible sprint windows, or unrecoverable item loss.",
      "Multiplayer Transition Safety: 15-second airlock evacuation warning auto-evacuates delayed, downed, or disconnected players into the safe staging zone of the new room without bypassing puzzle triggers.",
      "Physics Alignment: 1 abstract tile = 32 px. Normal jump apex = 71.5 px (2.23 tiles). Cooperative launch boost = 171.7 px (5.36 tiles) with v_boost = -520 px/s.",
      "Independent Room Presence During Backtracking: A Room 10 -> Room 9 transition must not move teammates out of Room 10. The 15-second airlock applies to forward progression only. Teammates remaining in Room 10 maintain independent room presence. Captured and disconnected player behavior is a documented rule requiring later runtime design and tests; leaving such players indefinitely in a room is not assumed to be automatically safe."
